# theTraffic. — environment template. Copy to web/.env.local. Never commit real values.

# ---- Browser-safe (inlined into the web bundle; prefix VITE_) ---------------------------------
# The web app needs NOTHING to run. There is no authentication, visitor-profile store or route
# planner: the research datasets are static JSON under web/public/data. The one server of ours the
# browser talks to is the grievance board (functions/). Posts do not request an identity, but their
# words, visible photo content, precise place and time may still identify someone.
#
# Only these eight VITE_ keys are read, each on its own (`import.meta.env.VITE_…`). Do not add other
# VITE_ values to the build environment: the build fails if a VITE_ key name or a credential-like value
# (KEY, TOKEN, SECRET, SUPABASE, MAPBOX, …) reaches a chunk — see vite.config.ts `envHygiene`.
# Every value is read at build time. On Vercel set them under Settings → Environment Variables (Production
# and Preview) and redeploy — docs/DEPLOYMENT.md § Vercel.

# Support page mailbox (mailto). The ONLY place the address exists — no built-in default since the
# 2026-09-09 security audit. Empty = the Support page has no e-mail channel and offers the clipboard alone.
VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# Basemap style (defaults to OpenFreeMap dark). Any MapLibre style JSON URL works; its origin is added
# to the Content Security Policy automatically.
VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL=
# Satellite imagery (XYZ raster template) and its attribution. Defaults to Esri World Imagery
# (keyless, attribution required). Point at Mapbox Satellite, Maxar, Bhuvan or any XYZ source instead;
# the origin is added to the CSP automatically.
VITE_SATELLITE_TILE_URL=
VITE_SATELLITE_ATTRIBUTION=

# Live signal timing. There is NO authorised live-timing adapter: the Mappls signal-timer programme
# (125+ smart signals, press release 25 Sep 2025) is a partnership / data-access opportunity only.
# Any value here is ignored with a console warning — the site never claims live coverage it lacks.
VITE_LIVE_TIMING_PROVIDER=

# Google Analytics 4 measurement id (G-XXXXXXXXXX). Empty = no analytics: nothing loads, nothing is sent,
# no Google host in the Content Security Policy. With an id the site sends one page view per screen
# (path only, no query string) and honours Global Privacy Control — see docs/PRIVACY.md.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# The grievance board's Worker origin (https). Empty = the project's own Worker
# (https://greenwave-bengaluru-backend.rork.app). The CSP connect-src / img-src follow the value.
VITE_GRIEVANCE_API_URL=
# The public origin of the site (https), written into the sitemap and canonical links.
# Empty = the official production site (https://www.thetraffic.in). Set it only when another canonical origin fronts the site.
VITE_SITE_URL=

# ---- Build-time only (read by vite.config.ts, never inlined) -----------------------------------
# Build stamp shown on the error panel. Default: the build's date and time, "2026-09-09 10:15Z" — on Vercel
# followed by the short commit, "2026-09-09 10:15Z · a1b2c3d" (VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA). A value here replaces it.
GW_BUILD=
# Extra origins for the Content Security Policy's connect-src / img-src, space separated — needed only
# when a custom style JSON references tile, glyph or sprite hosts other than its own.
GW_CSP_EXTRA_ORIGINS=

# ---- Worker only (project settings / wrangler secrets; never in source, never inlined) -------------
# Moderator passphrase for the grievance board: at least 20 characters. Empty = the moderation routes
# answer 503 and the board is append-only (nothing can be removed). Typed on /grievances → Moderator.
GRIEVANCE_ADMIN_KEY=
# Extra exact https origins allowed to read and write the board, space or comma separated.
# The public Rork site and local development hosts are built in. Do not use multi-tenant wildcards.
GRIEVANCE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# ---- Scripts only (never inlined) ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact the Overpass sync (scripts/sync-surveillance.ts) puts in its User-Agent, as Overpass etiquette
# asks: an e-mail address or a URL. Empty = the agent names the project only.
GW_CONTACT=

# ---- Retired integration variables ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The grievance Worker reads only the two variables above. Any MAPBOX_*, TOMTOM_*, SUPABASE_* or
# ADMIN_REVIEWER_EMAILS value still present in the project environment is read by nothing and must be
# deleted. Rotate any value that has appeared in a build, deployment, transcript or log
# (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, "Security").
